 :findings
  [{:id :trunk-entrance-forces-its-proof-config-into-the-graded-tree :severity :product-defect-class
    :what "namespace_split_io/execute! resolves :verification-profiles ONLY from (io/file workspace_root
           \".clj-surgeon.edn\"). The verb has no --config option. On a repository graded for byte-identity
           outside an authorised footprint, the only way to configure the trusted proof is to add a file the
           proof itself forbids."
    :evidence "Runner pilot before the cohort: the tool emitted a candidate that passed A1-A8, all eight B07
               preservation checks, both fresh-process load orders, focused + integration tests, full
               make runtests-once and kaocha — and was ROLLED BACK by its own proof on the single line
               'ADDED .clj-surgeon.edn'. Second pilot with the config moved out of the tree: committed,
               verification_complete true, proof_pending []."
    :cost-if-unfixed "Six arms would have failed on apparatus, not merit."
    :suggested-ratchet "Accept an explicit config path on the verb (mission/config-sources already models an
                        explicit-config source; execute! does not consult it), or resolve profiles from a
                        location outside workspace_root."}
   {:id :empty-commands-profile-is-configured-but-not-admitted :severity :usability
    :what "{:commands []} is reported in :configured_profiles but not in :admitted_profiles, and the verb
           refuses with 'not a synchronous, rollback-capable profile this workspace configures'. The
           admitted no-op shape is a vector of ONE ARGV VECTOR, [[\"/bin/true\"]]."
    :note "synchronous_verification/verification-preflight has an explicit commandless? branch, but it is
           unreachable because profile-capability returns nil for that spec first."}
   {:id :vacuous-verification-complete :severity :honesty
    :what "Under the no-op profile the receipt reports :verification_complete true and :proof_pending [] while
           the proof executed was /bin/true. Every D2-D6 caller independently flagged this in its own report
           and refused to treat the field as behavioural evidence — the brief warned them, and they complied."
    :consequence "b07-arms.md's pre-registered D success criterion (verification_complete true over the TRUSTED
                  profile) is met by D1 ONLY. D2-D6 are accepted on the runner's frozen oracle, exactly as N is."}
   {:id :in-call-acceptance-is-the-meter-hazard :severity :apparatus
    :what "D1 measured 341.6 s of candidate work, 243.9 s of which was the frozen acceptance oracle running
           inside the tool call. N never pays acceptance inside its clock. Left uncorrected this reads as
           D/N = 0.894 instead of 0.256 — the same arm, a 3.5x difference, decided entirely by where the
           acceptance boundary is drawn."
    :fix-applied "Amendment 1: no-op profile for D2-D6 so the call returns at emission and the runner grades
                  both arms with the same oracle. D1 retained as the labelled proof-inclusive diagnostic."}
   {:id :D-is-byte-deterministic-N-is-not :severity :finding-not-in-the-gate
    :what "All SIX D candidate patches are BYTE-IDENTICAL: sha256
           22848c8ceb87a902becd1e4f3e8f6b935da6f50b86d14e8fbcb7c095e35a038c, 1202 lines, six times.
           Stage 1's six NATIVE candidates were six DISTINCT patches (six distinct hashes, all accepted,
           semantically convergent but byte-divergent)."
    :why-it-matters "The D route removes caller-to-caller variance in the artefact entirely; the residual
                     spread in the D column (97.7-153.5 s) is orientation and reporting around a call whose
                     own elapsed time was 51.4-52.7 s in every no-op arm. Review cost of a fleet of D
                     changes is one diff, not N diffs. This was not a pre-registered clause and is not
                     counted toward the gate; it is recorded because it is the most decision-relevant thing
                     the cohort produced that the gate does not measure."
    :caveat "Determinism is not correctness. It is the same artefact each time BECAUSE the request pins the
             owners; a wrong request would be wrong identically six times."}
   {:id :native-floor-remains-saturated :severity :interpretation
    :what "All six D candidates were accepted, as were all six N candidates in stage 1. Neither arm makes
           correctness mistakes on this task, so D cannot win on quality here — only on wall."}]

